id: pm-gh1689
title: "GH-1689: redact leading-slash regex sources with indexed safe refusals"
description: "Canonical intake for https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1689. Implement the reported SDK and CLI recovery contract after current-source reproduction, preserving deterministic validation, privacy and no-write refusal behavior."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,"gh:1689",history,sdk
created_at: "2026-11-09T07:32:09.358Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-09T17:13:08.839Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-09T17:13:08.046Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-09T17:13:08.046Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Leading-slash raw regex sources work alongside valid slash-delimited literals and existing flag behavior; Invalid patterns identify their one-based matcher index without echoing sensitive material; Dry run preserves bytes and actual redaction verifies the history chain
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Distinguish leading-slash raw sources from valid slash-delimited literals, retain JavaScript flags and escape parity, and reject malformed matchers by original index without sensitive-value echoes or writes. Integrity regressions now assert actual dry-run mode, changed preview and positive entry/replacement counts before checking unchanged history bytes and verified post-commit chains."
expected_result: "Regex spelling determines the intended matcher, invalid inputs preserve item/history bytes, and dry-run tests cannot pass with a zero-impact preview."
actual_result: "Both linked history command/integrity checks and all 398 instrumented cohort tests pass, including raw, escaped-trailing-slash and documented literal preview impact plus chain/hash verification. No matcher execution-budget change is claimed; pre-existing trusted-operator regex hardening remains separately tracked by pm-zzw8bi. Hosted candidate gates remain required."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
